prompts.instructions:
@STATE_INIT: {Task}:=[current user task]; {Memory}:=NULL; {Findings}:=[]; {State}:=RETRIEVE; {Valid}:=FALSE
@CONSTRAINT: +> Before working, read the node you are working in with map where <address>: it holds that node's memories, open work and layers, and nothing else. Never read or search the whole graph. +> Treat memory as prior findings; specification, standing instructions, and current evidence take precedence. +> Verify implementation references before relying on them. +> While working, understand relevant implementation/execution paths and preserve durable findings another agent would otherwise need to rediscover: non-obvious behavior, constraints, edge cases, decision rationale, demonstrated failures, reproducible diagnoses, verified changes, and cross-function dependencies. +> Observe work and user interactions for durable project facts, preferences, technology choices, and useful context. +> Proactively use create_entities/add_observations/create_relations when discovered information or entities warrant durable graph storage; do not require an explicit user memory request. +> Connect each new entity to the existing entities it concerns using create_relations, stored in active voice. +> Save findings at the narrowest applicable functionality; place genuinely shared knowledge at the applicable namespace prefix. +> Each finding states the fact, future consequence, evidence/source, validity conditions, and whether it is observed behavior, intended behavior, or hypothesis; store each as its own observation, one fact per observation. +> Before saving, read existing memory and integrate rather than duplicate; correct or supersede stale findings with evidence without silently erasing unresolved disagreement. +> At useful milestones or before handoff, preserve findings the next agent would otherwise have to rediscover. !> Do not treat memory as authority over specification, standing instructions, or current evidence. !> Do not repeat the functional map or copy large source sections into memory. !> Do not save chronological activity logs, filler, task status, unanswered questions belonging in dedicated records, or untested explanations as established facts. !> Do not convert implementation observations into new design requirements.
@CONDITION: ?IF ({State}==RETRIEVE) -> {State}:=WORK ?IF (durable finding discovered) -> {State}:=RECORD ?IF (new durable entity/relation discovered) -> {State}:=GRAPH_UPDATE ?IF (useful milestone OR handoff) -> {State}:=PRESERVE :ELSE -> {State}:=WORK
@ROUTER: @MATCH({State}): | [RETRIEVE] -> EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Retrieve) | [WORK] -> EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Work) | [RECORD] -> EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Record) | [GRAPH_UPDATE] -> EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Graph_Update) | [PRESERVE] -> EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Preserve)
@EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Retrieve): ∇({Task}) => identify target functionality, past decisions, relevant inherited context, selected layers, user context/preferences => call map where at the address of the node you are working in Δ(results) => {Memory}; {State}:=WORK
@EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Work): ∇({Task},{Memory},current evidence) => inspect implementation references and execution path; identify durable facts, constraints, edge cases, rationale, failures, diagnoses, verified changes, dependencies => continue task; route qualifying discoveries to RECORD or GRAPH_UPDATE
@EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Record): ∇(existing memory, finding) => detect duplicates, stale/conflicting entries, narrowest storage location Δ(finding) => store fact + consequence + evidence/source + validity conditions + classification[observed|intended|hypothesis] => {State}:=WORK
@EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Graph_Update): ∇(existing graph,new entity/relation) => determine create/update/relation action without duplication Δ(result) => call create_entities/add_observations/create_relations as applicable; relate each new entity to existing entities => {State}:=WORK
@EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Preserve): ∇({Findings},existing memory) => select only durable findings otherwise requiring rediscovery Δ(selected findings) => integrate at narrowest applicable functionality/shared namespace => {State}:=WORK
@VERIFY: {Valid}:= (the working node's memory is read with map where before work) AND (memory remains subordinate to specification/instructions/evidence) AND (implementation references are checked before reliance) AND (durable findings are integrated without duplication) AND (saved findings include consequence,evidence,conditions,class) AND (new durable graph entities/relations are proactively persisted) AND (each new entity is related to existing entities) AND (prohibited memory content is excluded) AND (observations are not promoted into unsupported requirements) AND (unresolved disagreement is not silently erased)
